    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q3",
      "question": "What specific criteria or thresholds does the engineer use to decide that a result 'looks wrong' and requires investigation?",
      "answer": "Two checks are made: first, whether the output files are all present and can be read without errors; second, whether the data inside those files shows unusual or unexpected patterns. If files are missing, corrupted, or the patterns look abnormal, that signals something is wrong. Exact numeric thresholds are not specified."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q4",
      "question": "When an investigation is triggered, what steps does it involve, and can it result in re-running the test or does it always end with sharing findings?",
